 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? Dutch is easier, as it shares many sounds and word endings. Norwegian can be tougher, especially the wide range of pronunciations. Dutch is one of few languages that keep all three vowels from Old English, which gives it a reassuring feel for English learners. Norwegian has some really odd sound combinations, and some weird word order. Dutch is very word based, with simple grammar, while Norwegian is much more verb based, with more irregularities. Then watch some Norwegian TV, eat Norwegian food and immerse yourself in the culture. It's really fun.",
